# variants/kits/system/worker — the worker's thin host: containers, VMs, its own disks
#
# LEAF set: a flat list of atoms. See kits/core/base for the layering contract.
#
# The worker is core + podman + KVM: a job runs natively through `systemd-run` with
# the venv the host ships, and only the builds run in `systemd-nspawn`; podman is
# the container engine kept for container builds. KVM needs no package (the dist
# kernel carries kvm_amd/kvm_intel). smartmontools reads the machine's own disks.
#
# The worker also hosts bentoolkit's build VMs (`shidashi vm start --dev`, 2026-11-15):
# qemu brings qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-img and, as a dependency, the OVMF firmware;
# virtiofsd shares the pinned trees and the binpkg pool with the guest. They cannot be
# added to a running worker instead: the pool's binpkgs belong to the current pin, and
# on an image of an older one the install wants a new glibc and OpenSSL under a live sshd.
# libisoburn (xorriso) comes WITH qemu, never without: a node that has
# qemu-system-x86_64 runs its boot test natively (shidashi/vmrunner.py: native), and
# that path reads the ISO's bentoo/build.json with xorriso.

app-containers/podman
app-emulation/qemu
app-emulation/virtiofsd
dev-libs/libisoburn
sys-apps/smartmontools
